## Private API and exact computation boundary

```java
static byte[] ClassicNbtCanonicalBytes.encode(CompoundTag root, ClassicNbtLimits limits)
```

Input: exclusively caller-owned **stable** standard native compound data.
Return: freshly owned complete named-empty-root bytes. Null input/limits refuse
with NullPointerException; unsupported/unbounded/lossy/illegal data or oversized
helper budget refuses with IllegalArgumentException, before a partial result
escapes. These are computation exceptions, not new persisted failure IDs.

The helper first uses unchanged shape preflight, then unchanged BoundedNbt
lossless-emission preflight. Shape-first avoids the existing BoundedNbt foreign
list-child getId residual for the stable unsupported inputs exercised here.
This is not a callback sandbox for concurrent modification, native Item/Fluid
callbacks or arbitrary world objects. Encoder exact-class/depth/node/type/UTF/
list/byte rechecks bound its own work; it invokes no Tag.write/copy/equality,
registry/resource API or world operation.

Canonical framing preserves types, original strings/code units, array values
and list order; only compound keys use adopted K1. Root is type10 plus empty
modified-UTF name. Payloads use native DataOutput widths/String encoding, not
SNBT/JSON/compression/a new float protocol. No SHA256/domain prefix/hash-v1
producer is introduced. Refused typed-empty lists, noncanonical NaNs, overlong
UTF, foreign tags, End children and cycles are not normalized/emitted.

## Bounds / allocations / aliases

Limits constructor/constants are unchanged. Root separately authorized the
helper-only componentwise ceiling: no requested bytes/depth/nodes may exceed
existing REJECTED1,873,117/25/86,529; stricter positive budgets are accepted and
larger components refuse rather than clamp. Future callers still must supply
their exact individual-root ceilings (resources32,768/16/8,192), not the helper
maximum. See [clarified task](authority/CANONICAL-BYTES-TASK-CLARIFIED.md.raw.txt).

No encoder byte buffer exists until both preflights succeed. One fixed scratch
array has requested byte capacity and never grows. Success returns a distinct
trimmed copy no larger than that capacity: at most two such arrays overlap
(3,746,234 raw data bytes at maximum helper budget), plus bounded traversal/key
lists and JDK encoding/sort scratch. This is not a whole-JVM heap/performance
Gate claim. Names are length/budget-checked before sorting; DataOutput UTF
fields are limited to65,535 encoded bytes and checked against remaining output.
Temporary ordinary UTF-8 ordering arrays are not used as emitted names.

Shared-child versus independent equal tree values encode equally; no source
compound/list/array is reordered or detached by this helper. Returned arrays do
not alias input or another returned array. Mutation **between** calls changes
the new frame but not old output. Concurrent mutation **during** a call violates
the exclusive/stable-input precondition; structural/write rechecks are defense,
not an atomic snapshot/authority guarantee. No live native Tag is exported.

